  "aiContextParagraph": "The East Nusa Tenggara (NTT) police are currently investigating sexual assault allegations involving the Regent of Kupang, Yosef Lede. As part of the ongoing probe, authorities have searched the regent's official residence, collecting various items as evidence. While official proceedings continue, Yosef Lede remains classified by the police as a witness. The case has drawn broader attention to systemic issues regarding sexual violence, with the Indonesian Ombudsman recently releasing findings on dozens of sexual violence cases within Islamic boarding schools across eleven provinces. Furthermore, the Ministry of Basic and Secondary Education has reported thousands of child abuse cases occurring nationwide, largely within domestic environments. These developments occur as political parties, including Gerindra, have stated that they will take disciplinary action against members found guilty of such offenses, emphasizing the high-profile nature of the current inquiry involving a regional official.",
